-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021, current version as at 5 November 2026.
-- ORDER 6: COMMENCEMENT OF PROCEEDINGS (Division 1 general, Division 2 originating claim, Division 3 originating application).
-- Source: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore Statutes Online.
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here has been checked against the official text.
--
-- READING A RESULT.  JUST TRUE: the text says yes on these facts.  JUST FALSE: the text says no in its own words
-- (a flat negative, an "unless", an "if", "where" or "when" that is not met, "only if", a stated period that has run).
-- NOTHING: the text does not answer (a list not closed, a grant limited by its own wording, a scope limit with no "only",
-- a term or law outside the sources).  A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Order 3, Rule 2(1) is a caveat on every answer in these Rules and is not threaded as an input.
--
-- A Form is named by its number as a STRING (PLAN.md S-P1); the Forms themselves are in the practice directions.

-- ===========================================================================
§§ `Order 6, Division 1 -- general`
-- ===========================================================================

-- src:490 | 1. —(1) Unless these Rules or any written law otherwise provide, a claimant may commence proceedings by an originating claim or an originating
-- src:490 | application.
@ref O 6 r 1(1) (src:490)
GIVEN `these Rules or any written law otherwise provide` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 6 r 1(1) a claimant may commence proceedings by an originating claim or an originating application` MEANS
    IF `these Rules or any written law otherwise provide`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Unless these Rules or any written law otherwise provide"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:490 | (2) A claimant must commence proceedings by an originating claim where the material facts are in dispute.
@ref O 6 r 1(2) (src:490)
GIVEN `the material facts are in dispute` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 6 r 1(2) the claimant must commence proceedings by an originating claim` MEANS
    IF `the material facts are in dispute`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the material facts are in dispute"

-- src:491-496 | (3) A claimant must commence proceedings by an originating application where — ( a ) these Rules or any written law require it; ( b ) the proceedings
-- src:491-496 | concern an application made to the Court under any written law; or ( c ) the proceedings concern solely or primarily the construction of any written
-- src:491-496 | law, instrument or document or some question of law and the material facts are not in dispute.
@ref O 6 r 1(3) (src:491-496)
GIVEN `these Rules or any written law require an originating application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings concern an application made to the Court under a written law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings concern solely or primarily the construction of a written law, instrument or document or a question of law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the material facts are in dispute` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 6 r 1(3) the claimant must commence proceedings by an originating application` MEANS
    IF `these Rules or any written law require an originating application`
       OR `the proceedings concern an application made to the Court under a written law`
       OR (`the proceedings concern solely or primarily the construction of a written law, instrument or document or a question of law` AND (NOT `the material facts are in dispute`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where (a) these Rules or any written law require it; (b) the proceedings concern an application made to the Court under any written law; or (c) ... and the material facts are not in dispute"

-- Gathered by hand (ruling E1, option B, guidance for hand-gathering only): paragraphs (1) to (3) together.
-- Paragraphs (2) and (3) can both be met, and the text does not say which prevails.
DECLARE `o 6 r 1 the mode of commencing proceedings` IS ONE OF
    `o 6 r 1 an originating claim is required`
    `o 6 r 1 an originating application is required`
    `o 6 r 1 either mode may be used`
    `o 6 r 1 the text does not choose between the two modes`
    `o 6 r 1 not covered because these Rules or a written law otherwise provide`

-- src:490-496 | 1. —(1) Unless these Rules or any written law otherwise provide, a claimant may commence proceedings by an originating claim or an originating
-- src:490-496 | application. (2) A claimant must commence proceedings by an originating claim where the material facts are in dispute. (3) A claimant must commence
-- src:490-496 | proceedings by an originating application where — ( a ) these Rules or any written law require it; ( b ) the proceedings concern an application made
-- src:490-496 | to the Court under any written law; or ( c ) the proceedings concern solely or primarily the construction of any written law, instrument or document
-- src:490-496 | or some question of law and the material facts are not in dispute.
@ref O 6 r 1 (src:490-496)
GIVEN `these Rules or any written law otherwise provide` IS A BOOLEAN
      `these Rules or any written law require an originating application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings concern an application made to the Court under a written law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings concern solely or primarily the construction of a written law, instrument or document or a question of law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the material facts are in dispute` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `o 6 r 1 the mode of commencing proceedings`
`o 6 r 1 how the claimant commences proceedings` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`o 6 r 1(2) the claimant must commence proceedings by an originating claim` `the material facts are in dispute` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
           AND (`o 6 r 1(3) the claimant must commence proceedings by an originating application` `these Rules or any written law require an originating application` `the proceedings concern an application made to the Court under a written law` `the proceedings concern solely or primarily the construction of a written law, instrument or document or a question of law` `the material facts are in dispute` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
            THEN `o 6 r 1 the text does not choose between the two modes`
        IF `o 6 r 1(2) the claimant must commence proceedings by an originating claim` `the material facts are in dispute` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN `o 6 r 1 an originating claim is required`
        IF `o 6 r 1(3) the claimant must commence proceedings by an originating application` `these Rules or any written law require an originating application` `the proceedings concern an application made to the Court under a written law` `the proceedings concern solely or primarily the construction of a written law, instrument or document or a question of law` `the material facts are in dispute` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN `o 6 r 1 an originating application is required`
        IF `these Rules or any written law otherwise provide`
            THEN `o 6 r 1 not covered because these Rules or a written law otherwise provide`
        OTHERWISE `o 6 r 1 either mode may be used`

-- src:498 | 2. An originating claim or an originating application is deemed issued when the Registrar numbers, signs, seals and dates it.
@ref O 6 r 2 (src:498)
GIVEN `the Registrar numbers it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar signs it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar seals it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Registrar dates it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 6 r 2 the originating claim or originating application is deemed issued` MEANS
    IF `the Registrar numbers it` AND `the Registrar signs it` AND `the Registrar seals it` AND `the Registrar dates it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is deemed issued when the Registrar numbers, signs, seals and dates it" ("when" counts as "where")

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rule 3: how long the claim is valid for service
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- The months for which it is valid.  Served out of Singapore with the Court's approval under O 8 r 1(2), or where approval is
-- not required under O 8 r 1(3): 6 months; any other case: 3 months.
-- src:500-507 | 3. —(1) Subject to this Rule, an originating claim or an originating application is valid for service — ( a ) where the originating claim or
-- src:500-507 | originating application is to be served out of Singapore — (i) with the court’s approval under Order 8, Rule 1(2); or (ii) where the court’s approval
-- src:500-507 | is not required under Order 8, Rule 1(3), for 6 months beginning with the date of its issue; or ( b ) in any other case — for 3 months beginning with
-- src:500-507 | the date of its issue. [S 780/2023 wef 01/12/2023]
@ref O 6 r 3(1) (src:500-507)
GIVEN `it is to be served out of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court's approval has been obtained under Order 8, Rule 1(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court's approval is not required under Order 8, Rule 1(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`o 6 r 3(1) the number of months for which it is valid for service` MEANS
    IF `it is to be served out of Singapore` AND (`the Court's approval has been obtained under Order 8, Rule 1(2)` OR `the Court's approval is not required under Order 8, Rule 1(3)`)
    THEN 6
    ELSE 3

-- "for 6 months beginning with the date of its issue": the issue date is the first day, so the last day is the day before
-- the corresponding date N months later.  NOTHING when that month has no such day (the Rules do not say).
-- src:500-507 | 3. —(1) Subject to this Rule, an originating claim or an originating application is valid for service — ( a ) where the originating claim or
-- src:500-507 | originating application is to be served out of Singapore — (i) with the court’s approval under Order 8, Rule 1(2); or (ii) where the court’s approval
-- src:500-507 | is not required under Order 8, Rule 1(3), for 6 months beginning with the date of its issue; or ( b ) in any other case — for 3 months beginning with
-- src:500-507 | the date of its issue. [S 780/2023 wef 01/12/2023]
@ref O 6 r 3(1) (src:500-507)
GIVEN `the date of issue` IS A DATE
      `it is to be served out of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court's approval has been obtained under Order 8, Rule 1(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court's approval is not required under Order 8, Rule 1(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`o 6 r 3(1) the last day of validity for service` MEANS
    CONSIDER `o 3 r 3(2) a period of calendar months from a date ends on the corresponding day` `the date of issue` (`o 6 r 3(1) the number of months for which it is valid for service` `it is to be served out of Singapore` `the Court's approval has been obtained under Order 8, Rule 1(2)` `the Court's approval is not required under Order 8, Rule 1(3)`)
    WHEN JUST corresponding THEN JUST (`add months` `the date of issue` (`o 6 r 3(1) the number of months for which it is valid for service` `it is to be served out of Singapore` `the Court's approval has been obtained under Order 8, Rule 1(2)` `the Court's approval is not required under Order 8, Rule 1(3)`) MINUS 1)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the Rules do not say where a period of months ends when the later month has no corresponding day

-- Service on a day: inside the validity (as extended, if it was) the answer is JUST TRUE, after it JUST FALSE (a stated period).
-- `the date to which validity was extended` is NOTHING when it was not extended.
-- src:500-507 | 3. —(1) Subject to this Rule, an originating claim or an originating application is valid for service — ( a ) where the originating claim or
-- src:500-507 | originating application is to be served out of Singapore — (i) with the court’s approval under Order 8, Rule 1(2); or (ii) where the court’s approval
-- src:500-507 | is not required under Order 8, Rule 1(3), for 6 months beginning with the date of its issue; or ( b ) in any other case — for 3 months beginning with
-- src:500-507 | the date of its issue. [S 780/2023 wef 01/12/2023]
@ref O 6 r 3(1) (src:500-507)
GIVEN `the date of issue` IS A DATE
      `it is to be served out of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court's approval has been obtained under Order 8, Rule 1(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court's approval is not required under Order 8, Rule 1(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date to which the validity was extended` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date of service` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 6 r 3(1) the originating claim or originating application is valid for service on the day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date to which the validity was extended`
    WHEN JUST extended THEN
        IF `the date of service` AT MOST extended
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "valid for service ... for 6 months beginning with the date of its issue" and any extension under paragraphs (3) and (4)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        CONSIDER `o 6 r 3(1) the last day of validity for service` `the date of issue` `it is to be served out of Singapore` `the Court's approval has been obtained under Order 8, Rule 1(2)` `the Court's approval is not required under Order 8, Rule 1(3)`
        WHEN JUST lastDay THEN
            IF `the date of service` AT MOST lastDay
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "valid for service ... for 6 months beginning with the date of its issue ... in any other case — for 3 months beginning with the date of its issue"
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the last day of the period of months is not given by the Rules

