@ref O 6 r 3(2) (src:508)
GIVEN `it has not been served on all or any of the defendants` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 6 r 3(2) an application may be made to extend the validity` MEANS
    IF `it has not been served on all or any of the defendants`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if it has not been served on all or any of the defendants"

-- src:509 | (3) The Court may order the validity of the originating claim or originating application to be extended by a period beginning with the day next
-- src:509 | following that on which the originating claim or originating application would otherwise expire.
@ref O 6 r 3(3) (src:509)
GIVEN `the day on which it would otherwise expire` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`o 6 r 3(3) the day on which an extension of the validity begins` MEANS `the day on which it would otherwise expire` PLUS 1

-- src:510 | (4) Except in a special case, the Court may extend the validity of the originating claim or originating application only twice and by not more than 3
-- src:510 | months each time.
@ref O 6 r 3(4) (src:510)
GIVEN `it is a special case` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of extensions already ordered` IS A NUMBER
      `the months of the extension now sought` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 6 r 3(4) the Court may extend the validity` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is a special case`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "Except in a special case" lifts the limits and does not say what the Court may then do
        IF `the number of extensions already ordered` AT LEAST 2
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "only twice"
        IF `the months of the extension now sought` GREATER THAN 3
            THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "by not more than 3 months each time"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

