    IF `the claim is for personal injuries`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the claim is for personal injuries"

-- src:517 | (2) If the claim is for personal injuries, the claimant must annex a medical report and a statement of the special damages claimed to the originating
-- src:517 | claim.
@ref O 6 r 5(2) (src:517)
GIVEN `the claim is for personal injuries` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a report is annexed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the report substantiates all the personal injuries alleged in the statement of claim` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant proposes to adduce the report in evidence as part of the case at the trial` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a statement of the special damages claimed is annexed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement gives full particulars of the special damages claimed for expenses and losses already incurred` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement gives an estimate of any future expenses and losses` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 6 r 5(2) the originating claim has the medical report and the statement of special damages annexed` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the claim is for personal injuries`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the requirement is for a claim "for personal injuries"
        IF `a report is annexed` AND `a statement of the special damages claimed is annexed`
           AND `o 1 r 3(1) a report is a medical report` `the report substantiates all the personal injuries alleged in the statement of claim` `the claimant proposes to adduce the report in evidence as part of the case at the trial` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           AND `o 1 r 3(1) a statement is a statement of the special damages claimed` `the statement gives full particulars of the special damages claimed for expenses and losses already incurred` `the statement gives an estimate of any future expenses and losses` EQUALS JUST TRUE
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the claimant must annex a medical report and a statement of the special damages claimed to the originating claim"

DECLARE `o 6 r 5(3) how the originating claim is endorsed` IS ONE OF
    `o 6 r 5(3) endorsed generally with a concise description of the claim`
    `o 6 r 5(3) endorsed with a statement of claim in Form 9`
    `o 6 r 5(3) endorsed in some other way`

-- src:518 | (3) An originating claim may be endorsed generally with a concise description of the claim or with a statement of claim in Form 9.
@ref O 6 r 5(3) (src:518)
GIVEN endorsement IS A `o 6 r 5(3) how the originating claim is endorsed`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 6 r 5(3) the originating claim may be endorsed in that way` MEANS
    CONSIDER endorsement
    WHEN `o 6 r 5(3) endorsed generally with a concise description of the claim` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 6 r 5(3) endorsed with a statement of claim in Form 9` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 6 r 5(3) endorsed in some other way` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be endorsed generally ... or with a statement of claim in Form 9" says how it may, not how it may not

-- The seam of O 1 r 3(1): "originating claim" means an originating process by which an action is commenced in Court as described in Order 6, Rule 5.
-- Read here: a document not in Form 8 is JUST FALSE; one in Form 8 gets the answer of paragraph (3) on its endorsement, which is
-- NOTHING for an endorsement of some other kind (the Rule names two ways with no "only").
-- src:517-518 | An originating claim must be in Form 8. (2) If the claim is for personal injuries, the claimant must annex a medical report and a statement of the
-- src:517-518 | special damages claimed to the originating claim. (3) An originating claim may be endorsed generally with a concise description of the claim or with a
-- src:517-518 | statement of claim in Form 9.
@ref O 6 r 5 (src:517-518)
GIVEN `the Form number used` IS A STRING
      endorsement IS A `o 6 r 5(3) how the originating claim is endorsed`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 6 r 5 the document commences an action in Court as described` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the Form number used` EQUALS "8")
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An originating claim must be in Form 8" (O 1 r 3(1) hands the term to this Rule)
    ELSE `o 6 r 5(3) the originating claim may be endorsed in that way` endorsement -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a Form 8 document endorsed in some other way is not answered by "may be endorsed generally ... or with a statement of claim in Form 9"

