      `the day the originating claim is issued` IS A DATE
      `the day the limitation period for the cause of action expires` IS A DATE
      calendar IS A `Court calendar`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 6 r 5(4) the originating claim may be endorsed generally` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is a special case`
            THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "Except in a special case" lifts the limit and does not say that endorsing generally is then allowed
        IF `the day the limitation period for the cause of action expires` AT LEAST `o 3 r 3(3) the first day of a period after or from a date` `the day the originating claim is issued`
           AND `the day the limitation period for the cause of action expires` AT MOST `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` `o 6 r 5(4) the period for the limitation to expire after issue` `the day the originating claim is issued` calendar
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may be endorsed generally only if the limitation period for the cause of action will expire within 14 days after the originating claim is issued"

